2602:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c **** /**
2603:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @brief      Enters LP accel motion interrupt mode.
2604:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  The behavior of this feature is very different between the MPU6050 and the
2605:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  MPU6500. Each chip's version of this feature is explained below.
2606:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2607:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n MPU6050:
2608:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n When this mode is first enabled, the hardware captures a single accel
2609:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  sample, and subsequent samples are compared with this one to determine if
2610:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  the device is in motion. Therefore, whenever this "locked" sample needs to
2611:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  be changed, this function must be called again.
2612:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2613:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n The hardware motion threshold can be between 32mg and 8160mg in 32mg
2614:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  increments.
2615:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2616:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n Low-power accel mode supports the following frequencies:
2617:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n 1.25Hz, 5Hz, 20Hz, 40Hz
2618:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2619:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n MPU6500:
2620:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n Unlike the MPU6050 version, the hardware does not "lock in" a reference
2621:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  sample. The hardware monitors the accel data and detects any large change
2622:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  over a short period of time.
2623:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2624:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n The hardware motion threshold can be between 4mg and 1020mg in 4mg
2625:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  increments.
2626:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2627:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n MPU6500 Low-power accel mode supports the following frequencies:
2628:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n 1.25Hz, 2.5Hz, 5Hz, 10Hz, 20Hz, 40Hz, 80Hz, 160Hz, 320Hz, 640Hz
2629:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2630:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n\n NOTES:
2631:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n The driver will round down @e thresh to the nearest supported value if
2632:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  an unsupported threshold is selected.
2633:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n To select a fractional wake-up frequency, round down the value passed to
2634:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @e lpa_freq.
2635:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n The MPU6500 does not support a delay parameter. If this function is used
2636:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  for the MPU6500, the value passed to @e time will be ignored.
2637:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  \n To disable this mode, set @e lpa_freq to zero. The driver will restore
ARM GAS  C:\Users\FASCIN~1\AppData\Local\Temp\ccNBUjvk.s 			page 201


2638:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  the previous configuration.
2639:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *
2640:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @param[in]  thresh      Motion threshold in mg.
2641:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @param[in]  time        Duration in milliseconds that the accel data must
2642:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *                          exceed @e thresh before motion is reported.
2643:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @param[in]  lpa_freq    Minimum sampling rate, or zero to disable.
2644:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  *  @return     0 if successful.
2645:Modules/mpu6050/inv_mpu.c ****  */
